# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Why this file exists: the Dockerfile does `COPY web/ ./` (stage 1) and
# `COPY . .` (stage 2). Without a .dockerignore the host's stale, multi-GB
# web/node_modules would overwrite the clean `npm ci` result (wrong frontend
# deps in the release image), and local dev/working dirs would leak into the
# build layers and balloon the context. Keep this in sync with .gitignore.

# --- VCS ---
.git
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# --- Frontend deps & build artifacts (rebuilt inside the image) ---
# `**/node_modules` is the load-bearing entry: stage 1 runs `npm ci` and must
# NOT have it clobbered by the host copy. web/dist is produced by `npm run
# build` in-image and re-supplied to the Go stage via COPY --from.
**/node_modules
web/dist
web/.vite
web/playwright-report
web/test-results
web/playwright/.cache

# --- Go build output ---
bin/
out/

# --- Local agent/editor & working dirs (never ship) ---
.claude
.planning
.bench
.playwright-mcp
.remember
.codex

# --- Test / QA artifacts & screenshots ---
test-results
playwright-report
ui-test
*.png

# --- Reviewer / working markdown (not part of the build) ---
CODE-REVIEW-1.0.md
NEXT-SESSION-ISSUES.md
WALKTHROUGH-FINDINGS-2.md
WALKTHROUGH-FINDINGS-*.md
test-findings.md
test.md
tools.md

# --- Editor / OS cruft ---
.vscode
.idea
.editorconfig
*.swp
.DS_Store
